    "alert_id": "EX3_002",
    "title": "DTG hyperglycaemia risk factors require glucose monitoring",
    "message": "Guidelines require screening for hyperglycaemia risk factors before DTG use: age ≥40, BMI ≥25, hypertension history, or family history of DM. This patient has multiple risk factors — age 45, BMI 33 — warranting glucose monitoring every 3 months for the first 12 months. Fasting glucose today is 5.6 mmol/L (below the >6.95 threshold for contraindication). However, no 3-monthly glucose monitoring is documented since DTG initiation in January 2023, representing a monitoring gap. The elevated lipids (LDL 4.2, total cholesterol 6.4, triglycerides 2.3) further compound metabolic risk alongside obesity and hypothyroidism.",
    "issue_type": "monitoring_gap",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Continue DTG but implement 3-monthly glucose monitoring for the first 12 months. Address metabolic risk through weight management, thyroid optimisation, and lipid monitoring.",
